class:: MackeyGlass
summary:: Mackey–Glass delay differential system
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Flows
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/Chua

description::

The Mackey-Glass equation models physiological delayed feedback systems (such as the body's regulation of blood cells). Mathematically, it is a delayed differential equation (DDE), meaning the derivative of the current state depends on the state of the system at a specific time in the past. Conceptually, this creates a high-dimensional, smooth, and undulating chaotic flow that never truly repeats. It provides exceptionally deep, slowly wandering ambient modulation, behaving like a complex, natural terrain rather than a synthesized sequence.

Integrates the delay equation code::dx/dt = beta*delayedX/(1+delayedX.pow(n)) - gamma*x:: from Mackey and Glass's 1977 physiological-control model. It uses a circular history, cubic fractional-delay reads, and a Heun step.

The output is raw, unnormalized model state. code::tau/timeScale:: is the audio delay in seconds. Like link::Classes/DelayC::, MackeyGlass uses cubic delay access; unlike DelayC, the history is internal recurrence state rather than an input signal.

subsection:: Dynamics view

image::mackey-glass-dynamics.png#Left: a settled time trace at the documented defaults. Right: the delay portrait x(t) against x(t - 17), which exposes recurrence structure that a time trace alone hides.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: beta
Delayed feedback coefficient.
argument:: gamma
Current-state decay coefficient.
argument:: tau
Delay in model-time units; negative values become zero.
argument:: n
Feedback exponent. Combinations invalid for the current delayed state restore code::x0::.
argument:: x0
Initial state and complete reset-history value.
argument:: timeScale
Model-time units per audio second. Nonpositive values hold state.
argument:: maxDelaySeconds
Init-rate audio-history allocation, clipped to 0.001 through 60 seconds.
argument:: reset
Fill the history with code::x0:: on a rising edge.
returns:: One audio-rate raw state.

method:: kr
Control-rate version; one control duration is one integration interval.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ MackeyGlass.ar * 0.08 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(MackeyGlass.kr(timeScale: 4).linexp(0.4, 1.5, 80, 2000), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

code::
// High-Dimensional Ambient Ocean
(
{
    var mod, freq, sig, verb;
    // Delayed differential equations create deep, non-repeating swells
    mod = MackeyGlass.ar(SampleRate.ir/200);
    freq = mod.linexp(-1.5, 1.5, 50, 400);
    sig = Splay.ar(SinOsc.ar([freq, freq * 1.5, freq * 2.01]));
    verb = FreeVerb2.ar(sig[0], sig[1], 0.8, 0.9);
    verb * 0.2
}.play;
)
::
